# CQ2 - Which computational model (interatomic potential, thermodynamic model,
#        data-driven model) was used in a given simulation?
#
# PATH:   permitted process --obo:OBI_0000293 (has specified input)--> model INSTANCE;
#         model --rdf:type--> model class, closed under rdfs:subClassOf* to
#         go:GO_0000313 (computational model).
# PROCESS SCOPE: the query closes over an explicit root set instead of the whole
#         co:PMD_0000583 "computing process" subtree, so that non-simulation
#         computations (e.g. co:PMD_0025012 analytical calculation) are not treated
#         as simulations: co:PMD_0000933 simulation process (asserted subtree incl.
#         GO_0000300-305 and GO_0000310 via co:PMD_0000821), go:GO_0000306 density
#         functional theory calculation and go:GO_0000307 phase equilibrium
#         calculation. Deliberately excluded: go:GO_0000308 CALPHAD assessment
#         (the model is its specified OUTPUT; see CQ8) and go:GO_0000309 feature
#         generation (consumes structures/datasets, not computational models).
# EXPECTED RESULT COLUMNS:
#         ?simulation ?simClass - the run individual and its asserted class
#         ?model ?modelClass    - the model individual and its class
#                                 (go:GO_0000314 / 315 / 316 / 317 or go:GO_0000313)
# EXPECTED ROW COUNT on the 2.0.0-rc1 package: 4 - the force field of the melt-quench run
#         (one row per asserted run class), the thermodynamic model of the
#         devitrification-kinetics simulation and the data-driven property model.
# GRAPH ASSUMPTION: answers are computed on the ASSERTED graph only - rdfs:subClassOf*
#         traverses asserted subclass axioms; no OWL reasoning (including
#         owl:equivalentClass-based classification) is required or claimed. A reasoner
#         may widen the answer set; the expected count below refers to the asserted union.
# NOTES:  model components acting as inputs (e.g. dispersion corrections) are represented
#         at instance level as their own individuals; no extra class or relation is needed.
# VALIDATION: executed for the presentation-stage 2.0.0-rc1 package against the asserted
#         union of go_v2_candidate.ttl and the synthetic abox_meltquench_example.ttl
#         (Apache Jena arq and RDFLib, identical results).
PREFIX rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX obo:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/>
PREFIX co:   <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/>
PREFIX go:   <https://w3id.org/pmd/glass-ontology/>

SELECT DISTINCT ?simulation ?simClass ?model ?modelClass
WHERE {
  VALUES ?processRoot { co:PMD_0000933 go:GO_0000306 go:GO_0000307 }   # explicit root set (MODELING.md §5.8)

  ?simulation rdf:type ?simClass .
  ?simClass   rdfs:subClassOf* ?processRoot .     # closure from permitted roots only

  ?simulation obo:OBI_0000293 ?model .            # has specified input
  ?model      rdf:type ?modelClass .
  ?modelClass rdfs:subClassOf* go:GO_0000313 .    # computational model
}
ORDER BY ?simulation ?model
